[Music]  warm welcome to the program we begin in  the u.s where it's been revealed that  former trump administration official  john bolton was the target of a  murder-for-hire plot and a member of  iran's revolutionary guard is wanted by  the fbi on charges relating to the  alleged plan  we face a rising threat from  authoritarian regimes who seek to reach  beyond their own borders to commit acts  of repression including inside the  united states  this is an especially appalling example  of the government of iran perpetrating  egregious acts of transnational violence  in violation of u.s laws and our  national sovereignty  well our white house correspondent  kimberly halckett joins us live from  washington dc hi there kimberly good to  see you uh what are the details  well what we know is that the  person that has been charged with these  alleged crimes is still at large in fact  he was charged in abstentions 45 year  old iranian national by the name of  sharam pursafi he is also known by the  alias of mahdi  zai now what we do know is that he  allegedly tried to pay some three  hundred thousand dollars to assassinate  the former national security adviser  under the trump administration john  bolton and that this plot was allegedly  to take place either in washington dc  where we are standing or in the u.s  state of maryland which is just north of  here now this obviously was thwarted but  what we do know is that uh there are now  efforts by u.s officials to try and  detain and arrest this man and to see  him brought to justice now uh we can  tell you that this is not the first time  that the department of justice says that  it has uncovered plots against u.s  officials on u.s soil by the iranians  but certainly this is an egregious one  given the fact that this is such a  high-level u.s government official  and kimberly what's been the reaction  from john bolton himself  well we have heard from john bolton he  issued a statement and he has been  issuing comments uh to national  television stations  what he has been saying is not only is  he grateful to the u.s justice  department for stopping this plot but  also that he believes it underscores  the threat that the united states and  the wider sort of middle east faces as a  result of the instability and  destabilizing activity that iran is  causing in fact he says that  he believes that he is not the only one  that the ayatollahs in tehran are trying  to assassinate so this is the kind of  government that we have in iran that is  a quote from john bolton i can tell you  that that quote is consistent with some  of the testimony that was put forward by  the current secretary of state anthony  blinken back in april before the u.s  congress he said that he had knowledge  of threats by iran against u.s officials  both past and present  so this is significant we should also  tell you that the white house has  reacted to this latest  charges that have been laid against the  45 year old iranian national that did  try to  murder john bolton  what we can tell you is that the  national security adviser currently jake  sullivan has said the biden  administration will not waver to protect  and defend all americans against threats  of violence and terrorism should iran  attack any of our citizens iran will  face severe consequences and just very  quickly this does come at a particularly  precarious time given the fact that this  administration is trying to revive the  2015 agreement to limit iran's nuclear  program in exchange for sanctions relief  in fact the final text of that has been  sent to  following negotiations vienna to both  tehran and washington dc it's not clear  whether or not this is going to sort of  in any way foil those efforts to revive  that 2015 agreement that we should point  out donald trump pulled out of  may of 2018. so  this is certainly an uh  very interesting development and it  certainly could potentially complicate  those matters kimberly how could joining  us with the latest they're live from the  white house kimberly thank you  [Music]

